description:
MANDATORY release gate before NuGet publication. Requires explicit maintainer authorization and maintainer-provided NON-PRODUCTION sandbox AWS credentials. Do not start without both.
Design §19.1 (AUTHORITATIVE), §15 "Deployed validation".

Steps: using samples/web-functions (previous beads), build artifacts, deploy (artifacts stack → upload → app stack), run smoke.sh, then perform the update scenarios
(v2 artifacts → new revision active and endpoints moved; add then remove second distribution → statement added then removed), and destroy everything.

Must verify and record (status codes, revision IDs, policy JSON excerpts):
3.1 artifact deployment from both bucket-policy modes (Automatic owned bucket, ExternallyManaged pre-provisioned bucket);
3.2 function/revision/endpoints Active; redeploy with changed artifact activates a new revision and moves endpoints;
3.3 SigV4-signed request by the granted caller role → 2xx;
3.4 unsigned → 403; signed by an ungranted role → 403; signed for the second endpoint the role was not granted → 403;
3.5 through CloudFront → 2xx; direct unsigned to the IamAuth endpoint → 403;
3.6 get-resource-policy contains exactly the expected statements; second distribution adds a scoped statement; removing it removes the statement;
3.7 cross-account (only if a second sandbox account is available): ExternallyManaged grant + caller-account identity policy → success; without identity policy → denied; otherwise record "not verified";
3.8 Next.js page via CloudFront; ASP.NET Core endpoint (signed); Blazor Static SSR rendered page AND static asset served.
Also record: date, account alias (no account secrets), region, CDK version, library commit/working-tree state, and any criterion not verified.

Cleanup is required: run destroy.sh, verify no stacks, buckets (all versions), log groups, distributions, or roles remain; record verification.
This bead must NOT be closed on synthesis results alone. If any check fails, record it, file a bug bead linked to the responsible implementation bead, and leave this bead open.
Exclusions: production accounts, Sharedale resources, publishing, commits/PRs.
